laurel 3060: the resident set: a submission flagged MSM_SUBMIT_LAUREL_RESIDENT (0x01000000) lists only the buffers its command buffers index; the kernel takes every live buffer of the client as named (Turnip names the device's whole list at every submission anyway: 209,444 names in 84 submissions on the Mi A3 with live glass, about 2,500 a submission, 1176 us of kernel time each; docs/laurel_sprout/ios26-default-speed.md section 10). The push rules run over the client's own table (the same decisions), every live buffer gets the fence, the surfaces their drawn fence. Saved: the copyin of the list, its heap copy and three walks with a handle lookup each. GET_PARAM 0x7c answers 1: the client's self-check (Turnip patch 0110 reads it). A 5th stats line every 5 s: the walk's us a submission and how many submissions named the resident set. Kill switch gpuresident=0: the flag is ignored and the param answers 0. [V] compiles (snapshot build); NOT BOOTED.

